 "note": "QUICK START (the rewritten tutorial, TUTORIAL-REWRITE-DESIGN.md sec3). One hub: the rotation relay R in the middle, a pocket on each side. A's pocket on the left is H with N1 (T1, behind), N2 (T2, up toward the middle) and M (the common vat that gets the Machingoon, low toward the middle); B's is the mirror: BH, B1, B2 (T2), M2 (also RM). The sides meet only at R: each side's M has a fixed short deck to it, and R's rotation swings one short deck between B2 (r1, up at the start: the rival's side) and N2 (r2: the player's side). The rival's line BH -> B2 -> R -> M -> H is the fastest home-to-home route over the r1 deck, so firing R drops it. Last Stand inward only: the outer ring (both pockets, ring 1) falls first, the inner ring (R, M, M2, ring 0) stays. Names: H, N1, N2, M (Machingoon node), R (relay), BH, B1, B2, M2 (RM, the rival's equivalent of M); rings inner 0, outer 1.",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
